WEBVTT

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:12.450
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:36.010
<i>LINE.19  The Approaching Peak</i>

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:39.340
We still can't see the lead pack.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:39.870
Yeah.

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:41.490
Or Naruko-kun.

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:42.590
Yeah.

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:44.370
<i>Where and what is he doing?</i>

00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:49.000
<i>We just passed the Kumamoto Daiichi 
guys that just barely made it out.</i>

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:51.050
We should've caught up by now.

00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:53.250
But I don't see them.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:55.220
<i>Did you make it to the front?</i>

00:01:55.220 --> 00:02:00.010
<i>Does that mean you're fighting alone?</i>

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:03.590
Onoda, I'll help pull.

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:04.640
Let's go faster.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:07.270
Y-You can't! Fall back!

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:08.890
You're the ace, Imaizumi-kun!

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:11.780
You've been letting me conserve 
my strength until now!

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:13.440
It's okay! I'll pull!

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:19.860
I may be our ace, but I'm only half a man.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:21.120
Huh?

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:25.800
Until we started today, I thought 
I was a full-fledged ace.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.620
But during today's race, I came 
to the painful realization

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:31.090
that I'm still only half a man.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:32.380
I couldn't help my teammates.

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:35.250
I said awful things to my senior.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:36.460
My spirit broke immediately.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:40.380
Recover faster, Teshima-san!

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:41.800
Aren't you a climber?

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:47.850
Why are you smiling?

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:51.060
<i>What was that sound?</i>

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:53.360
But...

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:58.110
While I'm still a long way away from 
being a super ace like Kinjou-san,

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:01.940
I'm trying. Let me pull for now.

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:07.870
I'm not mature enough to sit 
back without doing anything.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:10.140
Imaizumi-kun...

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:15.000
<i>Onoda, you truly have saved me.</i>

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:20.010
Kaburagi-kun and Aoyagi-san 
have just rejoined the team!

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:24.130
<i>In this precarious situation, 
we got five of our members together.</i>

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:26.260
<i>Just like Onoda said.</i>

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:29.810
Um, Imaizumi-kun.

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:33.140
Aoyagi-san and Kaburagi-kun rejoined the team.

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:36.190
Y-Yeah, you're right. That's great.

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:39.440
They're amazing.

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:43.920
Now that there's five of us, I think 
we can catch up to Kumamoto Daiichi.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:46.950
And maybe even reach the 
lead pack where Naruko-kun is.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:48.950
Y-Yeah, maybe.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:51.260
It's all thanks to you.

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:54.480
<i>Thanks to me?</i>

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:56.830
<i>He's not making sense again.</i>

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:00.970
<i>I made an irremediable mistake.</i>

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:03.970
I've actually been thinking.

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:06.470
If you trace events back far enough,

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:10.000
sometimes you realize it actually 
started with someone small, you know?

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:10.980
It's about that.

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:17.020
The two of them rejoined the team when 
Teshima-san was coming up from behind

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:19.480
and Hakone Academy was leaving, 
during the first mountain.

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:22.490
I think it's because

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:27.280
you decided that we should wait.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:31.950
Wait, what? A-Am I wrong?

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:33.370
Sorry.

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:38.840
<i>Was that the right decision?</i>

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:42.970
<i>Is that the reason Aoyagi-san 
and Kaburagi caught up?</i>

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:47.470
<i>The reason there are five of us here now?</i>

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:54.270
<i>Onoda, how many times</i>

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:57.100
<i>are you going to save me?</i>

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:01.030
Onoda! You saved me!

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:01.690
Huh?

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:06.510
You can't know if you've made the right 
decision until you've seen the results.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:07.740
That's what you were trying to say.

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:11.080
If that's the case, then I'll
 work as hard as I can.

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:12.580
It's my only option!

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:15.630
We'll accelerate as quickly 
as we can while rotating.

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:19.080
Together, we'll catch up to 
the lead pack! To Naruko!

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:21.960
Yeah!

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:24.970
<b>Mountain
Line</b>

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:24.970
<b>Mountain
Line</b>

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.970
<b>Mountain
 Line</b>

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:29.850
I see.

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:34.220
Yes. Uh, we just got word 
from the club members below.

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:39.450
Ashikiba-san and Shinkai-kun are 
going after Kyoto Fushimi's ace.

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:43.860
Unfortunately, the race for the
 finish line has... already started...

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.880
I-I'm sorry.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:51.240
You came all the way out 
here to see the race, too.

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:54.910
What are you apologizing for? It's no matter.

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:59.420
That's just how road races are.

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:03.470
So you didn't get to go, Manami.

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:05.380
I know you.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:07.050
I'm sure you searched repeatedly

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:10.800
for opportunities to race against four-eyes.

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:13.440
It couldn't be helped.

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:15.640
But the race isn't over yet.

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:18.520
You'll have other opportunities.

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:20.770
Wh-Where are you going, Toudou-san?

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:24.110
<b>Elevation</b>

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:26.290
I came all the way here.

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:29.820
I'm heading down to the finish line
 to watch the race from there.

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:38.350
It's a bit too sad to see a mountain line
 race that isn't led by a climber.

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:42.090
His aura is incredible.

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:46.190
That's the Mountain God, 
the legendary Toudou-san.

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:49.010
I actually spoke to him.

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:53.650
<i>Hakone Academy has won all 
the number tags so far.</i>

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:57.680
<i>Since Izumida took the sprint, 
they've gained even more momentum.</i>

00:06:58.490 --> 00:07:02.690
<i>But there are other powerful teams 
who won't take that lying down.</i>

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:06.690
<i>They'll do whatever it takes to win.</i>

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:10.740
<i>This finish line won't be easily taken.</i>

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:15.010
<i>Kyoto Fushimi and Sohoku will 
make desperate plays for it, too.</i>

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:20.160
Approaching Kyoto Fushimi.

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:22.300
We might be able to catch up.

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:23.260
Move!

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:26.000
The redhead in front of 
them is slowing them down.

00:07:26.330 --> 00:07:27.460
Keep going.

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:29.920
Don't let your guard down until we catch up.

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:31.590
Or even after we do.

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:35.140
There's three more kilometers 
to the mountain line.

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:33.090
<b><i>Road Race</i>
Distance to Day 2
 Mountain Checkpoint</b>

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:37.290
Don't slow your pace, Yuto!

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:37.890
Yes, sir!

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:41.520
Hakone Academy is getting
 closer, Midousuji-kun!

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.340
Move, Naruko!

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:46.860
You stop, you purple seaweed!

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:49.360
Hakone Academy is getting closer!

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:54.350
They're not coming!
 Your teammates aren't coming!

00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:57.060
It's just a delusion!

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:59.330
A wish that won't come true!

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:04.380
Someone will come!
 I have a feeling they will.

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:07.960
It'll be real close and down to the wire,

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:12.290
but someone who doesn't think 
he's hot stuff will come!

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:15.640
Fine!

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:18.850
There's no getting through to you with words.

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:20.360
Come.

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:23.850
I'll have to use my body to make you

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:24.850
understand!

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:38.620
Bodies and bikes touch all the time while 
jockeying for position during a race.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:42.620
And I can't afford to spend all 
my time entertaining your

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:48.000
pointless determination and 
retaliatory spirit, Naruko!

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:52.110
#3, Naruko!

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:54.530
He hit the guard rail...

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:57.140
He fell! We did it!

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:02.020
Don't worry. He was at his limit, after all.

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:04.110
He would've fallen either way.

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:07.900
It was just a matter whether it was ten seconds 
from now or thirty seconds from now.

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:12.060
Come on, Sohoku. Damn it.

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:15.280
Wait up, Midousuji.

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:19.780
Kyoto Fushimi's #111 forced 
Sohoku out of his way.

00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:23.100
Sohoku's #3 is falling.

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:26.160
<i>He did everything he could, but Sohoku is...</i>

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:28.540
<i>Sohoku's Naruko...</i>

00:09:28.990 --> 00:09:31.100
I did my job.

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:37.300
I stuck to them, defended Sohoku's jersey,

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:41.930
and held them back until I reached my limit!

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:46.810
So come.

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:49.570
Come!

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:53.860
Come on, hotshot!

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:13.670
Naruko!

00:10:16.070 --> 00:10:22.250
How long were you gonna 
make me wait, hotshot?

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:27.600
I'm tagging out!

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:31.020
S-So...

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:34.860
Two Sohoku riders caught up!

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:37.440
Sohoku's Imaizumi...

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:40.660
<b><i>Road Race</i>
Distance to Day 2
 Mountain Checkpoint</b>

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:46.200
Two Sohoku riders caught up with two 
kilometers remaining to the mountain line!

00:10:46.820 --> 00:10:50.540
You... You're Crackizumi.

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:54.840
I thought you cracked 
with a grunt and a gasp.

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:58.090
You're supposed to have fallen behind!

00:10:58.810 --> 00:11:00.840
<i>I'm still only half a man.</i>

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:04.740
<i>I can't even move forward without help.</i>

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:07.060
<i>I can't make it this far 
on my strength alone.</i>

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:09.510
<i>So I'll say it.</i>

00:11:10.660 --> 00:11:13.370
<i>In order to inspire myself.</i>

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:17.280
<i>In order to accept that weighty 
responsibility on these shoulders.</i>

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:19.030
Ashikiba-san...

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:20.740
Midousuji...

00:11:21.330 --> 00:11:24.950
Allow me to reiterate. I am...

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:27.830
Sohoku's ace.

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:38.750
<i>What's with this guy?</i>

00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:43.720
<i>I know he cracked at the first peak.</i>

00:11:44.070 --> 00:11:45.820
<i>Crack, crack, crack, crack,</i>

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:47.580
<i>crack, crack, crack, crack.</i>

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:50.180
<i>So why? How did he do it?</i>

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:51.940
Crack!

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:54.690
Imaizumi-kun, how's Naruko-kun?

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:57.920
He's fine. There was still life in his eyes.

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:01.320
Teshima-san and the others will pick him up.

00:12:01.890 --> 00:12:04.190
He's pushed himself to his limit.

00:12:04.190 --> 00:12:06.740
Thanks to you, we caught up, Naruko.

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:11.060
You were supremely flashy!

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:11.580
Yeah!

00:12:12.030 --> 00:12:14.960
We'd better do our job, too.

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:17.670
We're carrying his and the team's hopes.

00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:19.610
Let's go, Onoda!

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:22.470
We'll take our jerseys 
to the finish line first!

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:23.130
Yeah!

00:12:27.210 --> 00:12:28.760
What are you doing?

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:32.260
Another fly caught up.

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:35.910
Why are you casually cycling?

00:12:35.910 --> 00:12:37.060
Come on.

00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:41.070
Pull ahead of them, Mizuta!

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:42.490
G-Got it!

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:47.050
It doesn't matter if your body falls apart!

00:12:47.050 --> 00:12:47.870
Y-Yeah?

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:50.870
Ace assistant #112 is accelerating!

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:52.540
Don't let them pull ahead, Yuto!

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:55.370
Hold on. Wait, Midousuji-kun.

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:58.290
I thought I heard you say 
it's fine if I fall apart.

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:00.620
I-I'm the captain.

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:02.610
I'm your talented launching pad.

00:13:02.610 --> 00:13:08.510
You're not thinking of disposing of me 
here like you did with Kiriya, are you?

00:13:11.590 --> 00:13:18.480
Mizuta-kun, you're still saying 
that this late in the game?

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:19.110
Huh?

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:22.570
Kyoto Fushimi's pace is falling!

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:25.530
We may be able to catch up to them now!

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:29.100
Mizuta-kun, you...

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:29.850
Yeah?

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:33.660
The reason I have you pull so hard...

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:34.540
Yes?

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:37.710
<b><i>Road Race</i>
Distance to Day 2
 Mountain Checkpoint</b>

00:13:36.220 --> 00:13:37.710
...is for that.

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:39.450
Huh? What?

00:13:39.450 --> 00:13:46.220
If you keep pulling me up 
this slope at full power,

00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:49.930
you'll be the King of the Mountain.

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:51.430
What?

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:58.060
<b>Mountain
Line</b>

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:58.060
<b>Mountain
Line</b>

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:56.890
No way! What?

00:13:56.890 --> 00:13:58.140
King of the Mountain?

00:13:58.510 --> 00:14:02.250
<i>Me? I'll have beaten Hakone Academy
 and Sohoku to be the</i>

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:05.820
<i>Inter-High's King of the Mountain?</i>

00:14:06.930 --> 00:14:08.820
They suddenly raised their pace again!

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:11.570
<i>I'm glad I stayed on the 
team for three years!</i>

00:14:11.570 --> 00:14:13.580
<i>The Inter-High's King of the Mountain!</i>

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:16.330
You're amazing, Mizuta-kun.

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:19.660
<i>Me, Mizuta Nobuyuki!</i>

00:14:21.300 --> 00:14:25.710
Despite everything you say, you really 
do care about me, Midousuji-kun!

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:31.530
<i>I'll use everything I can to win.</i>

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:33.310
Go, Zaku!

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:35.810
Show me your limit!

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:41.990
The lead they got earlier 
is really hurting us!

00:14:41.990 --> 00:14:44.480
We're so close, but we can't close the gap!

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:47.190
They're trying to hold this 
lead to the finish line!

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:50.330
After the mountain line 
is downhills and flats.

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:52.030
It'll be hard to close the gap there.

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:55.290
<b><i>Road Race</i>
Distance to Day 2
 Mountain Checkpoint</b>

00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:55.290
We have to catch up to them in the mountains.

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:57.290
Otherwise, the finish line...

00:14:57.740 --> 00:14:59.210
What should we do, Ashikiba-san?

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:05.380
<i>What is this rising pressure?</i>

00:15:05.740 --> 00:15:06.880
<i>That's...</i>

00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:12.120
We have to catch up in the mountains.

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:15.760
It's a 1,500-meter climb to the peak.

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:18.660
Can you do it, Onoda?

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:19.390
Yeah.

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:21.430
<i>The Mountain King!</i>

00:15:21.430 --> 00:15:22.770
<i>Onoda Sakamichi!</i>

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:29.180
Because Naruko-kun left by himself 
and worked so hard on his own,

00:15:29.180 --> 00:15:30.780
we made it this far!

00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:33.780
I'll pedal as hard as I can!

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:38.200
<i>He caught up in an instant!</i>

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:39.620
<i>Who is this guy?</i>

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:44.380
<i>He's way faster than during our 
race in the mountains earlier!</i>

00:15:45.980 --> 00:15:48.480
<i>Who's catching up?</i>

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:51.880
<i>Is it you, Sakamichi?</i>

00:15:58.260 --> 00:16:00.410
Did you see that, Midousuji?

00:16:00.410 --> 00:16:05.210
That was Naruko's Ultimate 
Flashy Miracle High Five!

00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:08.050
I just came up with the name.

00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:11.280
<i>The Mountain King is so fast!</i>

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:12.900
<i>He's trying to catch up?</i>

00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:18.370
<i>With 1,400 meters remaining to the peak?</i>

00:16:20.730 --> 00:16:27.380
<i>Are you going to destroy my lead, Sakamichi?</i>

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:30.170
<i>He's getting closer.</i>

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:35.940
<i>The little engine that's 
pulling me will overheat soon.</i>

00:16:35.940 --> 00:16:40.180
<i>Then I'll switch to my legs, the main engine.</i>

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:42.060
<i>How long will he last?</i>

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:46.440
<i>I have to make him last until the 
very last second by tricking him.</i>

00:16:46.760 --> 00:16:51.740
Mizuta-kun, there are lots 
of people at the peak.

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:52.440
Huh?

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:54.890
They're here to see you ride.

00:16:54.890 --> 00:16:58.580
To see you become King of the Mountain.

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:03.190
So you should go faster.

00:17:03.190 --> 00:17:04.520
Push your limits.

00:17:04.520 --> 00:17:05.870
King of the Mountain!

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:06.830
Go!

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:07.750
You can do it!

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:09.790
Look! Kyoto Fushimi's first!

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:11.090
It's third-year Mizuta!

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:13.480
<i>What? Someone said my name!</i>

00:17:13.480 --> 00:17:16.220
<i>I'm excited! I'm so excited!</i>

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:21.050
We're falling behind, Yuto!

00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:22.330
We'll use the group in front of us.

00:17:22.330 --> 00:17:24.560
Get behind Sohoku.

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:27.900
We'll stick behind them and 
catch up to the front together.

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:29.130
Hurry!

00:17:29.130 --> 00:17:30.150
<i>Mountain King...</i>

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:36.260
<i>He's definitely riding faster than he was 
during our first race in the mountains.</i>

00:17:36.730 --> 00:17:40.740
<i>Was he holding back? Is this the 
true strength of the Mountain King?</i>

00:17:41.380 --> 00:17:43.000
<i>Do guys like him exist?</i>

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:45.330
<i>Guys who ride faster when they're asked to</i>

00:17:45.860 --> 00:17:48.830
<i>than when they're racing for their own pride?</i>

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:51.760
Yuto!

00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:54.420
Y-Yes, sir. Sorry, Ashikiba-san.

00:17:56.870 --> 00:18:00.620
<i>I entered the Inter-High so I could 
race against the Mountain King.</i>

00:18:01.130 --> 00:18:04.520
<i>I thought I could beat him. I thought I did.</i>

00:18:04.990 --> 00:18:07.650
<i>I have to beat him,</i>

00:18:08.050 --> 00:18:10.650
<i>because I'm Shinkai Yuto.</i>

00:18:11.300 --> 00:18:13.820
<i>Because I'm not Shinkai Hayato.</i>

00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:17.230
If you don't stop thinking, 
we'll get left behind, Yuto!

00:18:18.100 --> 00:18:19.500
We're still on the climb.

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:20.350
But...

00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:22.450
the finish line is just ahead!

00:18:23.860 --> 00:18:25.200
<i>The finish line...</i>

00:18:25.550 --> 00:18:27.260
<i>That's right. Shoot.</i>

00:18:27.260 --> 00:18:28.290
<i>We're almost at the finish line.</i>

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:29.710
Sorry!

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:32.090
One more kilometer to the peak!

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:34.810
Who's going to become King of the Mountain?

00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:36.310
There's no telling anymore!

00:18:36.310 --> 00:18:38.680
Isn't this the race for the finish line?

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:42.720
#1 is pulling the three guys behind him!

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:43.570
Amazing!

00:18:43.570 --> 00:18:45.090
Tag #1...

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:52.560
He's the one who raced up Mt. Fuji first to 
lead Chiba's Sohoku to victory last year!

00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:54.980
That's Onoda Sakamichi!

00:18:55.330 --> 00:18:57.500
<i>It's hard, but I'll catch up to the front</i>

00:18:57.500 --> 00:19:00.780
<i>with our ace Imaizumi-kun in tow.</i>

00:19:01.510 --> 00:19:04.910
<i>As a climber, that's my job.</i>

00:19:06.180 --> 00:19:09.410
<i>Are you watching, Makishima-san?</i>

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:13.380
<i>Kinjou-san said you were in Japan.</i>

00:19:13.930 --> 00:19:16.400
<i>If you're watching somewhere—</i>

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:23.550
<i>No, if you read in the news later 
that we worked really hard,</i>

00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:28.390
<i>just that would make me happy.</i>

00:19:28.760 --> 00:19:30.330
He's almost caught up!

00:19:30.330 --> 00:19:32.070
Damn, Sohoku's amazing!

00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:33.490
Kyoto Fushimi, don't be beaten!

00:19:33.490 --> 00:19:34.400
Hakone Academy!

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:40.200
I left the others at the finish line

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:42.710
to come to the mountains alone,
 and here you are.

00:19:43.650 --> 00:19:50.290
Why do you always work so 
hard that I feel embarrassed?

00:19:52.530 --> 00:19:56.180
You're physically small, 
but you're <i>huge</i>, Onoda.

00:19:57.590 --> 00:20:00.810
Keep it up, Sakamichi.

00:20:01.830 --> 00:20:03.340
Stay on your path.

00:20:04.290 --> 00:20:07.890
It was hard. It took some time.

00:20:09.250 --> 00:20:10.750
<i>He really is amazing.</i>

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:13.100
<b>Road Race
Distance to Day 2
 Mountain Checkpoint</b>

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:15.860
But at 500 meters remaining,

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:19.100
we caught up to the front!

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:23.440
Sohoku and Hakone Academy 
caught up to Kyoto Fushimi!

00:20:23.440 --> 00:20:24.950
Amazing! Damn!

00:20:34.610 --> 00:20:36.830
We caught up.

00:20:40.250 --> 00:20:42.470
Thanks, Sakamichi.

00:20:43.390 --> 00:20:44.430
Sure.

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:52.300
Look! Sohoku's rotating Onoda back 
and sending someone else ahead!

00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:54.980
It's tag #2, their ace, Imaizumi!

00:20:55.450 --> 00:20:58.730
He's neck and neck with Kyoto Fushimi's ace!

00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:02.980
Come on, Midousuji.
 Attack whenever you're ready.

00:21:02.980 --> 00:21:06.860
I'll stop all your attempts.

00:21:06.860 --> 00:21:08.890
<i>What? What?</i>

00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:10.620
<i>What is this?</i>

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:12.980
<i>What is this pressure?</i>

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:15.080
<i>He's just Crackizumi!</i>

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:18.790
<i>O-Over here, too.</i>

00:21:19.220 --> 00:21:21.400
<i>Shinkai's little brother!</i>

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:23.290
We're ready, too.

00:21:23.290 --> 00:21:25.170
We'll stop you.

00:21:25.170 --> 00:21:28.550
<i>And behind him is</i>

00:21:29.190 --> 00:21:31.470
<i>their ace, Ashikiba!</i>

00:21:35.330 --> 00:21:38.370
<i>My only remaining option is...</i>

00:23:12.140 --> 00:23:15.030
Metamorphose...

00:23:15.030 --> 00:23:17.170
Princess, Princess.

00:23:17.170 --> 00:23:18.750
Mountain King?

00:23:19.490 --> 00:23:21.420
You're interested in this kind of thing?

00:23:21.420 --> 00:23:22.740
<i>He's so close!</i>

00:23:22.740 --> 00:23:26.610
Mountain King, do you have feminine desires?

00:23:26.610 --> 00:23:28.100
Does it make your heart pound?

00:23:28.100 --> 00:23:28.920
What?

00:23:30.340 --> 00:23:32.680
Shinkai-kun, do you like anime?

00:23:35.370 --> 00:23:36.770
<i>He's so close!</i>

00:23:36.770 --> 00:23:39.930
<i>NEXT LINE  King of the Mountain</i>

00:23:39.930 --> 00:23:44.940
